  "explain": "Q2 versus Q3 is the prefix rule of A3.4: an explicit negative at an established prefix gives No; an explicit denial behind an unknown step gives Unknown. Q3's second step is refuted by a timeless denial so that the query depends on no carried negative; the prefix alone decides. Q4 is the false-final-goal case through a strict library effect. Q7 shows that a verify question about executability in the final situation can itself depend on negative persistence; the fixture pins the diagnostic on the starting backend rather than an optimistic No. The source variants a_red and unknown_prefix are complete sources; no query adds a fact (A3.1).",
  "notes": "Amended 2026-09-11 (review R3, R8): the red-a fact moved from query-level additions into the source variant a_red; Q3 now uses a timeless denial instead of an unlisted negative-persistence dependency. c25 Q5 replays against a_red."
